# A synthetic reconstruction with hand-computable geometry.
#
# Not a neuron.  Every distance is a Pythagorean triple or an axis-aligned
# step so that segment lengths, branch points, tips, extent, reach and the
# length-weighted diameter distribution can each be worked out on paper and
# asserted exactly.  swclib._self_check() and test_neuron.py both read it.
#
# It exists because matching a published summary statistic does not pin a
# parser: a mis-summed length or a double-counted soma can still land near a
# plausible average.  This file is the ground truth instead.
#
#   soma      point 1 at the origin, radius 5            -> diameter 10
#   basal     1->2 length  5   (3,4,0)     diameter 2.0
#             2->3 length 12   (3,4,12)    diameter 2.0
#             3->4 length  3   (0,4,12)    diameter 1.0   tip
#             3->5 length  3   (6,4,12)    diameter 1.0   tip   (3 bifurcates)
#   axon      1->6 length  8   (0,0,-8)    diameter 0.5
#             6->7 length 12   (0,0,-20)   diameter 0.5   tip
#
#   basal 23, axon 20, total 43; reach 20 (point 7); extent 6 x 4 x 32;
#   diameters {2.0: 17 um, 1.0: 6 um, 0.5: 20 um} -> modal 0.5, share 20/43.
#
# id type    x    y     z  radius  parent
1 1 0 0 0 5.0 -1
2 3 3 4 0 1.0 1
3 3 3 4 12 1.0 2
4 3 0 4 12 0.5 3
5 3 6 4 12 0.5 3
6 2 0 0 -8 0.25 1
7 2 0 0 -20 0.25 6
